WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.107
You can do anything!

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:09.509
Paint a masterpiece in a minute,

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.978
learn every language in an hour,

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:15.348
build a multi-billion dollar
company overnight,

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.984
and rule the world by tomorrow!

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.531
Or is it because you're not using
your brain at its full potential?

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.934
This is 'What If,'

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.704
and here's what your brain
would be like at full capacity.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:42.208
The brain, to say the least,
is very complex.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:42.242
The brain, to say the least,
is very complex.
We've studied it for centuries, and we're
still learning more of its secrets today.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:46.579
We've studied it for centuries, and we're
still learning more of its secrets today.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:51.684
But be careful! The search for facts
can sometimes lead to fiction.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:01:00.960
Brain size relates more to proportion
than it does to intelligence.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.531
For example, here's your brain
next to a whale's.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:13.039
Your brain is smaller than a whale's
because your body is smaller.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:18.211
However, your brain is structured in a way
that enables you to survive, and succeed.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.988
We've seen what really
smart people can do. 

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:33.493
They inspire us through
art, music, and literature;

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.395
they change the odds in sports;

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.064
they come up with tools
to make our lives easier;

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:42.469
and they help organize society as a whole
to make us all more powerful

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:45.371
for better or for worse.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:49.709
With access to your brain's
full capacity, you're limitless.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.211
So what do you do?

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.947
First things first, you finally
get to solve the Rubik's cube

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.483
that's been collecting dust on your shelf.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:02:00.186
Call up your smartest friend, and
challenge them to a game of chess.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.188
Checkmate in two moves.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:07.861
When you're done being a smarty pants,
you'll be looking for a real challenge.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:10.563
Since, being smart means that
you won't be as stimulated

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.433
by the things that keep
us simpletons happy...

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.407
When you're limitless,
you don't have to choose.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.710
"Picasso was overrated!"

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.746
"Sorry I'm late, I was up
all night curing cancer!"

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:31.251
"...so I thought, well why not? And that's
how the time traveling toilet came to be!"

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.619
Okay, back up.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.989
What happens to your body when
you're dedicating all your brain's energy

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.059
to a creation, a cure, or a patent?

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.195
Your lungs breathing,
your heart beating,

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:45.064
your food digesting,
and your blood circulating

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.866
that's all your brain.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:52.305
Even if you could access 100% of
your brain's capacity, you couldn't use it.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:55.909
You would be limited by
your body's survival needs.

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.210
Remember when we asked,

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:08.354
The 10% thing is a myth; and it
probably comes from a simple confusion.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:13.159
Your brain is 10% neurons,
and 90% glial cells.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:16.529
There are different types of neurons
that take care of different functions,

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:21.434
but in general, your neurons enable you
to process and transmit information,

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:26.773
while your glial cells surround your neurons,
providing them with support and insulation.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:34.914
Your brain has just as many
neurons as Albert Einstein's did!

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:47.827
Maintain healthy habits;
that's the smart thing to do!

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:53.266
And, of course, it's a no brainer!

